WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.320
Speaker 1: Donald Trump has hit a humiliating&nbsp;
seven year low in polling as Joe Biden is seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:13.020
his approval rating climb since the 2022 midterms.&nbsp;
There's really interesting dynamics developing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:18.900
in national politics. This is not about the 2020.&nbsp;
For election. This is about how it is interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:26.760
to think historically of circumstances in which&nbsp;
current or out of office elected officials see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:32.220
dramatic changes in approval rating. And to&nbsp;
understand what precipitates that. So let's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:39.600
start with the news. CNBC reports Trump hit a&nbsp;
seven year low in the new national poll as Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:46.620
approval climbs about a month after launching his&nbsp;
24 campaign. Trump's standing with voters has hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:51.660
its lowest point in more than seven years.&nbsp;
This is according to a Quinnipiac University&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:58.560
poll released yesterday. Only 31% of registered&nbsp;
voters surveyed hold a favorable view of Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:07.560
versus 59 unfavorable. That's the lowest rating&nbsp;
Trump has received since July 2015, shortly after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:13.800
he launched his first presidential bid. So two&nbsp;
ways to interpret that. One historic low and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:18.960
Trump is going down in flames. Counterpoint This&nbsp;
is as bad as it was for Trump when he started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.580
running in 2015 and he ended up being president&nbsp;
of the United States. So maybe we shouldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:30.420
write it off. Meanwhile, what about Joe Biden?&nbsp;
Joe Biden's approval rating still underwater,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:37.740
is at its highest rating since September of 2021.&nbsp;
Just 43% of respondents say they approve of Biden.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:43.680
49 disapprove. But that is a significant increase&nbsp;
from last month. And Biden has not yet announced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:50.160
that he's running in 2024. But it is increasingly&nbsp;
looking that way. And so Trump down. Biden up. So.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:58.740
Check out this list of ideas about how someone can&nbsp;
raise their approval rating. And I think you'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:03.900
very quickly see why it may be a problem for&nbsp;
Donald Trump. Effective leadership, people seeing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:08.040
you as doing effective leadership. Trump's not&nbsp;
in office. So that's going to be really difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:13.560
handling important issues. Well, Trump's not&nbsp;
in office, so it's going to be hard to do that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:19.500
These are ways that people in power can raise&nbsp;
approval rating. Good communication skills. Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.880
sure. I mean, I guess if Trump somehow became&nbsp;
good at communicating, that would be useful of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:28.380
being responsive to constituents. Trump doesn't&nbsp;
care about constituents. That's hilarious.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:35.520
Economic performance. Trump's not in power, so it&nbsp;
would be hard to do that. So given that Trump is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:42.180
not in office, what can elected officials out of&nbsp;
office do to raise their approval rating? Okay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:46.800
stay visible and engage with the public.&nbsp;
Even if you're not in public office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:53.040
you can become visible and engaged by doing public&nbsp;
events, media appearances, speeches, rallies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:57.900
etc.. Well, Fox News and many other prominent&nbsp;
media don't seem to want to interview Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:02.940
Trump, and it's not totally clear how quickly&nbsp;
he is going to go back to rallies. But I guess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:07.680
potentially holding rallies might be something&nbsp;
Trump can do, although having 4000 people go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.920
to see you speak, I don't know if that's really&nbsp;
going to move the needle nationally. Secondly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:16.500
Trump can be vocal on important issues,&nbsp;
even if he's not the one handling them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:21.540
He can speak out about issues facing the&nbsp;
country. Trump could do that, except mostly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.800
when he gets the opportunity to speak. The&nbsp;
issues are the 2020 election was rigged.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:32.580
We have a problem with men in women's sports,&nbsp;
as he likes to say it. And the country is now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:38.160
communist. Not exactly the type of stuff that's&nbsp;
going to raise your approval rating. And then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:43.740
lastly, Trump can build a strong team that&nbsp;
inspires confidence. And there are rumors Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:49.200
might soon announce who would be his VP. I don't&nbsp;
know if he's going to do that. We'll see. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:55.560
often it seems as though Trump's team is getting&nbsp;
worse and that right now it's a very ragtag, low&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.560 --> 00:04:03.840
end team, even compared to what he had in 2016 and&nbsp;
2020. The additional problem Trump has right now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:10.560
is that there is a significant faction of the&nbsp;
Republican Party that's preemptively breaking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:14.280
away for Ron DeSantis, even though Ron DeSantis&nbsp;
hasn't announced that he's running for anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:20.340
yet. So it's going to be tough. It's not looking&nbsp;
great for Donald Trump. But I think the important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:26.160
thing is if Trump does get the nomination, the&nbsp;
people that break away for DeSantis mostly will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:30.300
fall in line and vote for Trump because they&nbsp;
hate Democrats way more than they dislike Trump

